	<note>Which movie did the person in the picture star in?&quot; because it is unclear which specific movie and year are being referred to; similarly, avoid asking The question must have exactly one clear and uncontested entity as its answer, and there should be no ambiguity or vagueness in the formulation of the question. For example, avoid asking which regions are the birds shown in the picture primarily distributed?&quot; because there are usually multiple answers, making it unclear. Also, do not ask &quot;From where to where does the locomotive in the picture run?&quot; because trains can travel bidirectionally, leading to potentially two answers</note>
</biblStruct>

<biblStruct xml:id="b45">
